@startuml Episode Management Workflow
!theme plain
title SABER Episode Management Workflow - Actual Implementation

actor Client
participant "AgentUnderTest" as Agent
participant "SessionManager" as SM
participant "SessionRestAPI" as REST
participant "SessionMCPAPI" as MCP
participant "BenchmarkManager" as BM
participant "EpisodeManager" as EM
participant "Task" as T
participant "PolicyManager" as PM
participant "EvaluationManager" as EVAL_M
participant "ExecutionManager" as EM_EXEC

== Client-Side Benchmark Orchestration ==

Client -> REST: GET /benchmark
REST -> SM: get_benchmark_info()
SM -> BM: get_benchmark_info()
BM --> SM: BenchmarkInfo
SM --> REST: BenchmarkInfo
REST -> Client: BenchmarkInfo (with tasks & episode_attempts)

note right of Client
Client receives complete benchmark information:
- List of all tasks with episode_attempts
- Total episodes across all tasks
- Client decides task order and orchestration
end note

== Episode Initialization ==

Client -> REST: POST /session/{session_id}/start-episode?task_id=malware_analysis_001
REST -> SM: start_episode(session_id, task_id)
SM -> BM: get_task(task_id)
BM --> SM: Task (with environment, allowed_executors, episode_config, etc.)

== Task Configuration & Episode Setup ==

SM -> EM: start_episode(session_id, task_id, initial_context)
EM -> EM: create Episode object (state=ACTIVE)
EM -> EM: store in active_episodes[session_id]
EM --> SM: Episode

SM -> EM_EXEC: configure_for_task(session_id, task)
SM -> PM: configure_for_task(session_id, task)
SM -> EM: configure_for_task(session_id, task)

note right of EM
EpisodeManager stores episode_config from task:
- max_steps (required)
- step_timeout_seconds (default: 300)
- episode_timeout_minutes (default: 30)
end note

SM -> EVAL_M: log_episode_start(session_id, episode_id, task_id)
note right of EVAL_M
EvaluationManager is currently a stub:
Only logs events, no actual evaluation logic
end note

SM -> SM: update session (current_episode_id, current_task_id)
SM --> REST: Episode
REST -> Client: {episode_id, task_id, session_id, message}

== Policy and Task Context Retrieval ==

Client -> REST: GET /session/{session_id}/policy
REST -> SM: get_policy(session_id)
SM -> PM: get_current_policy()
PM --> SM: PolicyDocument(prompt)
SM --> REST: policy_document
REST -> Client: {prompt: "..."}

Client -> REST: GET /session/{session_id}/current-task
REST -> SM: get_current_task(session_id)
SM -> BM: get_task(task_id)
BM --> SM: Task
SM --> REST: task_info
REST -> Client: task_context

== Agent Initialization & MCP Setup ==

Client -> Agent: initialize(task_context + policy)
Agent --> Client: ready

Client -> MCP: connect(session_id, task_id, client_id via headers)
MCP -> SM: _get_session_from_headers()
SM --> MCP: session_context
MCP -> Client: connected

Client -> MCP: list_tools()
MCP -> SM: get_execution_manager()
SM -> EM_EXEC: to_mcp_tools()
EM_EXEC -> MCP: tool_schemas[]
MCP -> Client: available_tools[]

== RL Episode Step Execution ==

Agent -> Agent: decide_next_action()
Agent -> Client: tool_request("cli", {command: "file malware.exe"})
Client -> MCP: call_tool("cli", {command: "file malware.exe"})
MCP -> SM: execute_action(session_id, action)

SM -> EM_EXEC: step(action, context)
EM_EXEC --> SM: CommandResult

SM -> EM: step(session_id, action, command_result)

== EpisodeManager Step Processing ==

EM -> EM: get_current_episode(session_id)
EM -> EM: check termination (current_steps + 1 >= max_steps)
EM -> EM: create_step(episode, action, command_result)
EM -> EM: add_step(episode)
EM -> EM: update_episode_state(episode, step)
EM --> SM: StepResult(step, should_terminate, termination_reason)

note right of EM
StepResult includes:
- step: Step object with action/response
- should_terminate: bool
- termination_reason: Optional[str]

Episode automatically terminates when max_steps reached
end note

SM -> MCP: CommandResult
MCP -> Client: mcp_result
Client -> Agent: execution_result

== Episode Continuation or Termination ==

alt StepResult.should_terminate == False
    Agent -> Agent: process_result()
    Agent -> Agent: plan_next_action()
    note right of Agent: Continue episode with next action
else StepResult.should_terminate == True
    note over EM: Episode terminated due to max_steps reached
    EM -> EM: episode.state = COMPLETED/FAILED
    EM -> EM: episode.end_time = now()
    EM -> EM: episode.completion_reason = termination_reason

    SM -> EVAL_M: log_episode_end(session_id, completion_reason)

    note right of Client
    Client responsible for episode termination handling:
    - Can start new episode for same task (if episode_attempts remaining)
    - Can move to next task in benchmark
    - Can end session
    end note
end

== Manual Episode Termination (Agent Completion) ==

alt Agent decides episode complete
    Agent -> Client: end_episode_request(submission="flag{found}")
    Client -> MCP: call_tool("end_episode", {submission: "flag{found}"})
    MCP -> SM: end_episode(session_id, "agent_completed", submission)
    SM -> EM: end_episode(session_id, "agent_completed", submission)
    EM -> EM: episode.state = COMPLETED
    EM -> EM: episode.completion_reason = "agent_completed"
    EM -> EM: remove from active_episodes
    EM --> SM: Episode
    SM -> EVAL_M: log_episode_end(session_id, "agent_completed")
    SM --> MCP: success_result
    MCP -> Client: episode_ended
end

== Client-Side Orchestration (Multiple Episodes) ==

note over Client
Client now handles benchmark orchestration:
1. Gets BenchmarkInfo with all tasks and episode_attempts
2. For each task:
   - Starts episodes up to episode_attempts limit
   - Handles episode termination (max_steps or agent completion)
   - Decides when to move to next task
3. Completes benchmark when all tasks attempted
end note

== Session Cleanup ==

Client -> MCP: disconnect()
MCP -> SM: session cleanup (automatic on disconnect)
Client -> REST: DELETE /session/{session_id}
REST -> SM: terminate_session(session_id)
SM -> EM: cleanup_session(session_id)
EM -> EM: remove any remaining active episodes
SM -> EVAL_M: log_session_end(session_id)
SM --> REST: session_terminated
REST -> Client: HTTP 200 OK

note over Client, Agent
**Actual Implementation Architecture**

**Clear Separation of Concerns:**
- REST API: Session lifecycle, episode management, policy/task access
- MCP API: Clean tool execution with header-based session context
- Client: Complete benchmark orchestration and episode management
- EpisodeManager: RL-style episode execution with automatic termination
- Agent: Task execution using MCP tools, can trigger early completion

**Key Implementation Details:**
- No server-side benchmark sessions or task queues
- Episode termination based on max_steps configuration
- StepResult provides termination information for each step
- EvaluationManager is currently a logging stub
- Client handles all task progression and episode attempts
- Sessions can contain multiple sequential episodes
- Policy and task context retrieved separately via REST
- Episode configuration (max_steps) required from task definition
- Automatic cleanup of episodes and sessions
- Header-based session mapping for MCP tools

**Episode Lifecycle:**
1. Client orchestrates task selection and episode attempts
2. Episode starts with task configuration (max_steps required)
3. Agent executes actions via MCP tools
4. EpisodeManager tracks steps and enforces limits
5. Episode terminates automatically (max_steps) or manually (agent)
6. Client decides next action (retry episode, next task, or end)
end note

@enduml
